  "question": {
    "html": "<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"N\"></span> molecules of an ideal gas are contained in a container that is sealed with a movable piston. Initially, the volume of the gas is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"100\"></span> cm<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{3}\"></span>. When the piston is moved, the average kinetic energy of the gas molecules is reduced by <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"50\"></span> %, while the pressure in the container does not change. What is the new volume of the gas?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"25\"></span> cm<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{3}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"50\"></span> cm<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{3}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"200\"></span> cm<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{3}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"400\"></span> cm<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{3}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
